id: decisions/005-field-obligation
title: "Which fields a record may leave off"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'field-obligation'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: field-obligation
axis_gloss: "whether a field must be present for a record to be valid, or may be left off"
poles:
  a: mandatory-field-set
  b: optional-field-set
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: full
leverage: 34.8
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(29) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  When a record leaves a field off, does that mean the field was optional or
  that the record is incomplete, and should every contract say which fields are
  which?

why_it_matters: >
  The written rule makes goals optional (a Yawn needs no target, an Observation
  needs no Yawn), but nothing says which fields a record must carry, so
  migrations/node.yawn ships a proof block with no status and the Homebase
  contract declares two of the four authority flags. A bot reading a record
  cannot tell silence from permission until this is answered; a child Yawn
  inherits either a required list or a guess.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    12 judgments sit at mandatory-field-set (0 authored) and 17 at
    optional-field-set (7 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether Dave treats a classifier's summary, sentiment and severity as
    observations that must be present, or as inferences that may be absent; J0342
    is the only record that answers, and it answers by omitting an optional list.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      Every key in a contract's declared shape is required unless the contract lists
      it under optional:. A record missing a shape key is invalid.
    cost: "An optional: list added to every contract that has a shape (state-transition, canonical-extension provenance_shape, folder-node node_shape, feedback-intake); target_condition and Observation attachment moved into those lists to preserve the authored rule."
    risk: "Records that were valid yesterday fail today; the 50 v0-seed files with sparse shapes need grandfathering."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A new scripts/validate-record-shape.mjs in npm run validate that reads each contract's shape and optional list and rejects records missing a required key; start with node.yawn files against core/folder-node.yawn node_shape."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0109"
      - "J0110"
      - "J0342"
      - "J0518"
      - "J0558"
      - "J0572"
  - name: B
    description: >
      Every key is optional unless the contract lists it under required:. A record
      carrying only what it knows is complete.
    cost: "A required: list in every contract that lacks one (canonical-extension provenance_shape has none; folder-node node_shape has none)."
    risk: "Recovery fields (proof.status, stop_condition, unintended_effects, authority flags) get omitted silently, which is exactly the J0329 and J0429 case."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Same validator as A, reading required: instead of optional:; extend tests/interface-contracts.test.mjs to assert desktop-homebase-v1 declares all four authority flags."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0219"
      - "J0268"
      - "J0299"
      - "J0329"
      - "J0408"
      - "J0429"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Goal fields are optional; recovery fields are required. A record need not
      carry a target, a move, or a parent Yawn. It must carry every field that says
      how it can fail or be undone: proof.status, reversibility, stop_condition,
      residual_lacuna_refs, unintended_effects, and all four authority flags
      wherever one appears. Every contract carries a required: list naming these;
      model-derived classifications (summary, sentiment, severity) are never in it.
    cost: "One rule in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn; a required: list in each contract; proof.status added to migrations/node.yawn; two flags added to interface/desktop-homebase-v1.yawn; database/feedback-intake.yawn required_fields split into observed and inferred."
    risk: "The line between goal and recovery fields needs a judgment call per contract; some fields (target_conditions in a family record) sit on both sides."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Extend tests/state-substrate-v1.test.mjs (which already asserts optional-target fixtures cover non-goal Yawns) with the recovery-field check; extend tests/interface-contracts.test.mjs to require all four authority flags on desktop-homebase-v1; a node-shape validator in npm run validate that rejects a proof block without status."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0109"
      - "J0110"
      - "J0219"
      - "J0299"
      - "J0329"
      - "J0429"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.65
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    The two authored judgments (J0219, J0299) only ever made goal fields optional,
    and the tests implement exactly that: 'Observation is valid without Target,
    Move, or Yawn promotion' and 'optional-target fixtures cover non-goal Yawns'
    both pass. The revealed mandatory judgments (J0109, J0110) require recovery
    and falsification fields, not goals. These do not conflict; the gap is that no
    contract states its required list, which is why J0268, J0329 and J0429 read as
    silent omissions rather than choices. C writes down the split the executable
    layer already draws. It is close because J0342 (thirteen required intake
    fields including model output) is the one place the artifacts require
    inference as if it were fact, and C would reverse it.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/proof-and-boundary.yawn names which fields are recovery fields and states they are required wherever the record can act or be acted on"
    - "migrations/node.yawn carries proof.status and interface/desktop-homebase-v1.yawn declares persistenceAuthorized and modelCallAuthorized, asserted by tests/interface-contracts.test.mjs"
    - "A validator in npm run validate rejects a node.yawn whose proof block lacks status, and passes"
    - "database/feedback-intake.yawn separates required observed fields from optional inferred fields"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new contract lands with a required_fields list that names model-derived
    output and no optional list, or a node.yawn without proof.status passes npm
    run validate.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0109"
  - "J0110"
  - "J0342"
  - "J0518"
  - "J0558"
  - "J0572"
  - "J0219"
  - "J0268"
  - "J0299"
  - "J0329"
  - "J0408"
  - "J0429"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
